<title>INDIA: Indian silver loses on new arrivals, gold subdued.</title>
<headline>Indian silver loses on new arrivals, gold subdued.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silver prices opened on a quiet note but fresh arrivals of imported silver dragged prices downward towards the close, dealer said.</p>
<p>Gold opened on a weak note but scattered seasonal enquiries at the lower level trimmed early losses towards the close.</p>
<p>Gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) settled 100 rupees lower at 60,500 rupees per piece.</p>
<p>&quot;The sentiment was subdued at the close on reports of sliding global prices and traders were expecting market to remain subdued next week,&quot; one broker said.  </p>
